Lab 9: Configure Canary Release Strategy
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Understand the concept and benefits of canary release deployments
Configure canary release strategy using Istio service mesh routing rules
Implement traffic splitting between stable and canary versions of a microservice
Monitor the health of both versions during a deployment
Execute rollback procedures when issues are detected in the canary version
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Kubernetes concepts (pods, services, deployments)
Familiarity with microservices architecture principles
Knowledge of YAML configuration files
Understanding of HTTP traffic routing concepts
Experience with command-line interface operations
