Task 1: Deploy Stable and Canary Versions with Traffic Splitting
Subtask 1.1: Deploy the Initial Stable Version
Create the application namespace and enable sidecar injection:
kubectl create namespace canary-demo
kubectl label namespace canary-demo istio-injection=enabled
Create stable-app.yaml:
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: product-service-stable
  namespace: canary-demo
  labels:
    app: product-service
    version: stable
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: product-service
      version: stable
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: product-service
        version: stable
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: product-service
        image: nginx:1.20
        ports:
        - containerPort: 80
        env:
        - name: VERSION
          value: "stable-v1.0"
        volumeMounts:
        - name: html-content
          mountPath: /usr/share/nginx/html
      volumes:
      - name: html-content
        configMap:
          name: stable-content
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: stable-content
  namespace: canary-demo
data:
  index.html: |
    <!DOCTYPE html>
    <html>
    <head><title>Product Service - Stable Version</title></head>
    <body>
        <h1>Product Service</h1>
        <h2>Version: Stable v1.0</h2>
        <p>This is the stable production version</p>
        <div style="background-color: green; color: white; padding: 10px;">
            Status: STABLE
        </div>
    </body>
    </html>
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: product-service
  namespace: canary-demo
  labels:
    app: product-service
spec:
  selector:
    app: product-service
  ports:
  - port: 80
    targetPort: 80
    name: http
Apply and verify:
kubectl apply -f stable-app.yaml
kubectl get pods -n canary-demo -l version=stable
kubectl get svc -n canary-demo
Deliverable: kubectl get pods -n canary-demo -l version=stable shows 2 pods in Running state with 2/2 containers ready (app container plus Istio sidecar).

